# binarybeachio: shell scripts, Jinja templates, and Dockerfiles that get
# executed (or built into) inside the Linux container MUST stay LF-terminated,
# regardless of the cloning host's core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a
# Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true converts these to CRLF; a shebang
# becomes `#!/bin/sh\r` (invalid path), and the container crashloops with the
# misleading `exec /start.sh: no such file or directory`. The bb-vaultwarden-fork
# `mine.1` build burned us this way 2026-04-30 — pin LF as a pre-flight on
# every bb-* fork.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.j2 text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
